# Milestone: v1.0-rc stdlib-completeness (zero-divisor rebaselined v0.13.5)
# Covers: % modulo operator (Integer and Float), zero-divisor error.
#
# The `a % b` source form desugars to a.'%'(b) in the parser (front's work).
# The '%' native methods on Integer/Float live in src/stdlib/atoms.c.
#
# v0.13.5: modulo-by-zero now raises a catchable DivByZero (legacy
# "modulo by 0") instead of a TypeError — legacy-conformant with float.cc
# operator% (`if (rhs) fmod(...) else RAISE("modulo by 0")`).
7 % 3
[00000000] 1
10 % 2
[00000001] 0
7.5 % 2.0
[00000002] 1.5
5 % 0
[00000003] !!! DivByZero: modulo by 0
